    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caupōnĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		caupo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a retail
			shopkeeper</i>, or <i>to an innkeeper</i>: puer, <i>a shop</i> or <i>tavern boy</i>, <i>waiter</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Poen. 5, 5, 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taberna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					23, 2, 43</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">33, 7, 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes exercere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. 1,
					7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caupōnĭum</span></b> , ii,
				n., <i>tavern furniture</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33,
				7, 15</span></i> pr.</div>
